🧠 MNIST GAN - End-to-End Machine Learning Pipeline
This Google Colab notebook implements an end-to-end Generative Adversarial Network (GAN) pipeline using the MNIST dataset (loaded from CSV). The goal is to train a GAN to generate new, realistic handwritten digits.

📌 Key Features
📥 Data Loading: MNIST data loaded via Pandas from a public CSV URL

🧹 Preprocessing: Normalized pixel values to [-1, 1] and reshaped for Conv2D layers

🧠 Generator & Discriminator:

Generator creates fake handwritten digits from random noise

Discriminator learns to distinguish real from fake digits

⚙️ Training Loop:

Custom training function with loss calculations and backpropagation

Uses BinaryCrossEntropy loss and Adam optimizer

📸 Visualization:

Intermediate images generated after each epoch to visualize training progress

🔍 Inspection:

Generator architecture and key attributes (input/output shape, layers) printed for documentation and debugging

🎯 Technologies Used
Python, TensorFlow (Keras), Pandas, Matplotlib

Google Colab (free GPU/TPU)

📈 Output
Generator progressively improves image quality with each epoch

Final output shows synthetic handwritten digits generated from random noise vectors

✅ Usage
Just open the notebook in Google Colab, run all cells, and watch your GAN learn to draw digits!
